[
  "ACT 1: COLD OPEN & PERSONAL GROUNDING [00:00 - 03:00]\nScene: 01. Starting Soon -> 02. Monologue / Full Camera\n\nWelcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter The AI Horizon & The Observable Control Plane. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers in Chicago were building grassroots rooms to escape corporate silos. Today we rewatch Episode 37: Community Panel & Open Roundtable from Live Stream Roundtable (2026).",
  "ACT 2: SETTING THE HISTORICAL SCENE [03:00 - 08:00]\nScene: 02. Monologue / Full Camera\n\nAn open invitational panel bringing together original Chicago organizers, apprentices, and modern platform engineers. When we recorded this in 2026, there were no corporate sponsor filters. Developers were meeting after hours, sharing hard-won lessons on deliberate practice and system boundaries.",
  "ACT 3: THE CORE INQUIRY: THE SOUND ABOVE [08:00 - 14:00]\nScene: 02. Monologue / Full Camera -> 04. Split Screen\n\nWhat is the permanent legacy of the Software Craftsmanship movement? What will we pass down to the generation learning to code in 2030? Who inspired Community Panel & Open Roundtable before they stepped onto this stage? What records were playing in the background when this movement formed?",
  "ACT 4: HALLWAY REWATCH & VIDEO REACTION [14:00 - 28:00]\nScene: 03. Reaction - Video Focus\n\nRoll archive footage (YouTube ID: ). Watch for the unvarnished hallway exchanges, the emphasis on craft over speed, and the sheer enthusiasm of engineers taking responsibility for their software.",
  "ACT 5: THE AI-ERA PARALLEL & TERMINAL WORKBENCH [28:00 - 40:00]\nScene: 05. Workbench - Code & Terminal\n\nThe tools will change completely; the human commitment to learning about people, one conversation at a time, remains unbroken. When implementation is cheap, verification and clarity become everything. We cannot accept the mirage of competence. Let us examine the terminal contracts directly.",
  "ACT 6: COMMUNITY CODA, OUTRO & NEXT STREAM [40:00 - 45:00]\nScene: 08. Outro & Next Stream\n\nThank you for joining today's session. Full transcripts, provenance notes, and companion research are available at just3ws.com. In our next broadcast, we explore Episode 0. Until next time, keep your feedback loops fast and your code humane."
]